{"name":"Dermastamp","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":18,"casual":{"lead":["A dermastamp is a small stamp-like microneedling tool used at home. Looksmax forum users apply it to skin, under-eye lines and brows, sometimes alongside minoxidil, aiming for smoother skin and fuller brows.","It presses a pad of short needles into the skin, creating tiny punctures that microneedling proponents say trigger repair and help topicals absorb. Microneedling generally has published studies, and lab work on related microneedle devices has looked at improving drug delivery through skin; no appearance trials of the stamp itself were found."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Users stamp the target area at home, usually as a routine paired with a topical."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Infection is a recognised concern with non-sterile or untrained microneedling. Device quality and hygiene vary."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Intradermal Delivery of an Immunomodulator for Basal Cell Carcinoma; Expanding the Mechanistic Insight into Solid Microneedle-Enhanced Delivery of Hydrophobic Molecules.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32510228/","source":"Molecular pharmaceutics","year":2020,"cites":39,"kind":null},{"title":"Application of microneedles for the treatment of nodular basal cell carcinoma","url":"https://europepmc.org/article/ETH/836401","source":"University of Nottingham","year":2021,"cites":0,"kind":null},{"title":"Squeezing Dynamic Mechanism of High-Viscosity Droplet and its Application for Adhesive Dispensing in Sub-Nanoliter Resolution.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31661827/","source":"Micromachines","year":2019,"cites":null,"kind":null}],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"derma stamp/ roller","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/derma-stamp-roller.1791277/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251229071727/https://looksmax.org/threads/derma-stamp-ro